    "reason": "The changelog entry [ev-d83aa8e2cc23] only says logs RBAC is now enforced by default. The linked PR [ev-4120f7386ac5][ev-a09101c7e15d] has only an empty checklist and gives no details. [ev-88b2096256eb] shows that the PR changed docs/operator-manual/upgrading/2.14-3.0.md and argocd-cm.yaml, but that text is not in the evidence. Without it, nothing says whether principals without a logs grant lose log access (permission-lost) or whether the old behaviour can be kept through a setting. The proposed statement that users 'may now be denied logs' describes losing access but labels it behavior-change, so the right kind can't be settled until the 2.14→3.0 upgrade-guide section on logs RBAC (the key, the old default and the effect on existing roles) is available.",
